          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_11_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.446,
            0.632,
            0.494
          ],
          "content": "**Note that the pair (1, 4) is different from (4, 1). (Why?) So, the number of possible outcomes = 6 × 6 = 36.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.501,
            0.9,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": "**(i) The outcomes favourable to the event ‘the sum of the two numbers is** $8 ^ { \\circ }$ **d**enoted **by E, are: (2, 6), (3, 5), (4, 4), (5, 3), (6, 2) (see Fig. 14.3)** i.e., the number of outcomes favourable to $\\mathrm { E } = 5$ **Hence,** $P(E) = \\frac{5}{36}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.298,
            0.572,
            0.368,
            0.617
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_11_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.638,
            0.901,
            0.73
          ],
          "content": "**(ii) As you can see from Fig. 14.3, there is no outcome favourable to the event F, ‘the sum of two numbers is 13’.** 0 **So, P(F) =** 0 **36**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.746,
            0.9,
            0.787
          ],
          "content": "(iii) As you can see from Fig. 14.3, all the outcomes are favourable to the event $\\mathrm { G }$ **‘sum of two numbers** $\\leq 1 2 ^ { \\star }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.809,
            0.188,
            0.827
          ],
          "content": "**So,**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.416,
            0.796,
            0.566,
            0.837
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm { P ( G ) }   =   \\frac { 3 6 } { 3 6 }   =   1",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_12.jpg"
        },
